{title: Goodbye World Goodbye}
{key: C}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]I've told all my [F7]troubles [C]goodbye,
[C]Goodbye to each [F7]tear and each [C]sigh.
[G]This world where I roam can[C]not be my [A7]home,
[D7]I'm bound for that home in the [G]sky.
[C]I walk and I [F7]talk with my [C]Lord,
[C]I feast every [F7]day on His [C]word,
[G]Heaven is near [C]and I can't stay [A7]here
[F]Goodbye [G]world, [C]goodbye

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Now don't you [E7]weep for me when I'm gone
[E7]For I won't have to leave here alone
[A7]And when I hear that last trump't sound
[D7]My feet won't stay on the [G]ground
[C]I'm gonna rise with a [F7]shout, gonna [C7]fly,
[C]Gonna rise with my [F7]Lord in the [C7]sky,
[G]Heaven is near and [C]I can't stay [A7]here,
[F]Goodbye [G]world, [C]goodbye.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]I won't have the [F7]blues any[C]more
[C]When I step across [F7]to that [C]shore
[G]I'll never pine, just [C]leave them [A7]behind
[D7]Heartaches and tears forever[G]more
[C]A day may maybe [F7]two then good[C]bye
[C]Tomorrow I'll [F7]rise up and [C]fly
[G]Heaven is near [C]and I can't stay [A7]here
[F]Goodbye [G]world, [C]goodbye
